# GitHub Copilot Instructions

Follow the canonical repository workflow in `AGENTS.md` and inherit its `## Development-Harness Boundary`.

## Orchestrated-Worker Protocol

Protocol marker: `ORCHESTRATED_WORKER_CONTINUITY_V1`.

The persistent development orchestrator keeps the user-facing chat open and delegates bounded repository work to fresh workers when the host supports them. Each mutating worker runs `node .harness/run.mjs session`, reads the small harness state and relevant routed docs, then runs `doctor`, `status`, and `next` before edits. Allow one mutating worker at a time; read-only explorers may run in parallel.

Use `checkpoint --reason worker_yield` for normal completion and `checkpoint --reason needs_input` for a user-input pause. Return a concise result or question and yield. Reserve `handoff` for a true worker transfer; the orchestrator delegates its exact resume command to a fresh worker without consuming the implementation packet. Open a fresh Copilot chat or task only when subagent delegation is unavailable.

Use `.harness/run.mjs` for state changes and require successful `verify` evidence before completion. Product-runtime agents and orchestration remain application-owned and independent of `.harness/`.
